{
  "opening": "This release introduces several new features and critical bug fixes to the parsing library, enhancing both usability and accuracy. Key additions include a new letters matcher, support for slice access on results, and improved handling of various numeric formats. Additionally, performance and correctness issues regarding case sensitivity, alignment, and brace matching have been resolved.",
  "requirements": [
    {
      "id": "m02",
      "text": "The 'letters' format specifier must match alphabetic characters only, excluding digits which are previously matched by 'w'. Using this specifier in a pattern should correctly extract string segments containing only letters."
    },
    {
      "id": "m03",
      "text": "Result instances must support the `__contains__` method, allowing users to check if a specific value or field exists within the result. This enables direct boolean checks like `value in result` for parsed data."
    },
    {
      "id": "m05",
      "text": "The parser must ensure that parts enclosed in braces are fully matched before processing, preventing partial matches when braces are unbalanced or malformed. Invalid brace structures should now trigger appropriate errors rather than silently producing incorrect results."
    },
    {
      "id": "m11",
      "text": "FixedTzOffset must correctly handle timezone offset parsing as per the reported bug fix, ensuring accurate time zone representation. The offset values should be interpreted consistently with standard timezone definitions."
    },
    {
      "id": "m15",
      "text": "The parser must correctly handle Fortran-formatted floating-point numbers, recognizing their specific syntax during parsing. This ensures that such numeric strings are converted to float objects without error."
    },
    {
      "id": "m17",
      "text": "Hexadecimal, binary, and octal number parsing must be corrected to properly identify signed numbers and detect bases automatically when not explicitly specified. The int_convert function should accept an optional base argument and correctly apply sign specifiers in regex patterns for integer types."
    },
    {
      "id": "m23",
      "text": "The findall function must respect the case_sensitive parameter, ensuring that pattern matching behavior aligns with the specified case sensitivity setting. Case-insensitive searches should ignore letter casing, while case-sensitive ones must match exactly."
    },
    {
      "id": "m25",
      "text": "Left- and center-aligned search operations must consume input up to the next space character, improving alignment parsing accuracy. Various internal conversions and pattern matching behaviors across multiple public names should reflect these alignment corrections."
    },
    {
      "id": "m28",
      "text": "Result objects must support slice access, allowing users to retrieve subsets of parsed values using standard Python slicing syntax. This provides a convenient way to extract multiple fields from a single result instance."
    }
  ],
  "closing": "Please verify that all public APIs behave as described above, particularly focusing on edge cases in numeric parsing and alignment logic. Ensure backward compatibility is maintained where no breaking changes were intended."
}
